  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# The Issue\n\nCurrently, it's impossible to constrain an object to your viewport—meaning that we are unable to add cameras or lights to the player's viewport. This would be extremely useful for things such as adding user interfaces that are made up of 2D meshes instead of forcing us to use a Screenspace shader. Simply parenting or constraining GameObjects to the Head does not work as it is too jittery and is clamped on desktop (& possibly VR? Not sure.)\n\n# Proposed Solution\n\nAdd a Component called `VRC Viewport Constraint`. This would act similarly to a Parent Constraint, but instead of having multiple sources the only possible source would be the player's Viewport.",
